$ weave daemon --help
Manage the weave Host, which runs agents so their threads outlive the TUI

Usage: weave daemon <COMMAND>

Commands:
  run        Serve in the foreground until stopped (for launchd or systemd, or to watch its log)
  start      Start the Host in the background, if it isn't running
  stop       Stop the Host and its agents once running turns end. Threads it had open can be reopened later
  restart    Stop the Host if it's running, once running turns end, then start it again: after rebuilding weave
  status     What the Host is running
  install    Run the Host as a service (launchd's on macOS, systemd's on Linux): kept running, with no idle exit
  uninstall  Remove the service `install` wrote, stopping the Host
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help

