$ weave smoke --help
Run one prompt headlessly and print every ACP event the agent sends

Usage: weave smoke [OPTIONS] [PROMPT]... [-- <COMMAND>...]

Arguments:
  [PROMPT]...
          The prompt to send. Before the agent's arguments, whose custom command comes last, after `--`

  [COMMAND]...
          A custom agent command and its arguments, given after `--`

Options:
      --agent <AGENT>
          Agent to launch: a preset (claude, codex, gemini), one defined in the config file, or an ACP registry agent's id (`weave agents` lists them)

      --trace [<TRACE>]
          Append a protocol trace of the agent to this file, viewable with agent-client-protocol-trace-viewer. Through the weave Host, which writes the trace in its own directory and says where, give it without a file

      --config <CONFIG>
          Config file. Defaults to ~/.config/weave/config.toml

      --cwd <CWD>
          Thread working directory. Defaults to the current directory

      --add-dir <DIR>
          An extra workspace root for the thread; repeatable. Needs agent support

      --no-fs
          Don't offer the agent fs/read_text_file and fs/write_text_file

      --no-terminal
          Don't offer the agent terminals for running commands

      --approve <KINDS>
          Tool kinds to allow, comma-separated: read, edit, delete, move, search, execute, think, fetch, switch_mode, other; or all. Everything else is rejected

  -h, --help
          Print help

$ weave login --help
Sign in to the agent with one of the methods it offers

Usage: weave login [OPTIONS] [-- <COMMAND>...]

Arguments:
  [COMMAND]...
          A custom agent command and its arguments, given after `--`

Options:
      --agent <AGENT>
          Agent to launch: a preset (claude, codex, gemini), one defined in the config file, or an ACP registry agent's id (`weave agents` lists them)

      --trace [<TRACE>]
          Append a protocol trace of the agent to this file, viewable with agent-client-protocol-trace-viewer. Through the weave Host, which writes the trace in its own directory and says where, give it without a file

      --config <CONFIG>
          Config file. Defaults to ~/.config/weave/config.toml

      --method <METHOD>
          The sign-in method's id; asked for when omitted

  -h, --help
          Print help

$ weave logout --help
Sign out of the agent, if it supports signing out

Usage: weave logout [OPTIONS] [-- <COMMAND>...]

Arguments:
  [COMMAND]...
          A custom agent command and its arguments, given after `--`

Options:
      --agent <AGENT>
          Agent to launch: a preset (claude, codex, gemini), one defined in the config file, or an ACP registry agent's id (`weave agents` lists them)

      --trace [<TRACE>]
          Append a protocol trace of the agent to this file, viewable with agent-client-protocol-trace-viewer. Through the weave Host, which writes the trace in its own directory and says where, give it without a file

      --config <CONFIG>
          Config file. Defaults to ~/.config/weave/config.toml

  -h, --help
          Print help

$ weave agents --help
List the agents `--agent` accepts: presets, the config's, and the ACP registry's

Usage: weave agents [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --refresh
          Fetch the ACP registry again rather than use the copy cached within the last day

      --config <CONFIG>
          Config file. Defaults to ~/.config/weave/config.toml

  -h, --help
          Print help
